# GENERATED TRAINING CORPORA. `backend/dataset/**/scenarios.jsonl` (191 files, 1.5 GB on
# disk, ~41 MB packed) is already tracked and is NOT removed — it was produced by
# `generate_dataset_enhanced.py`, which sets no random seed and can call an LLM, so it is
# NOT reproducible: deleting it loses ~500,000 scenarios that cannot be regenerated
# identically. See `docs/engineering/large-assets.md`.
#
# These patterns stop the NEXT corpus from landing in git. Anything new goes to an object
# store or a release artefact.
backend/dataset/**/*.generated.jsonl
backend/dataset/**/train.jsonl
backend/dataset/**/validation.jsonl
backend/dataset/**/training_data.jsonl
backend/dataset/**/*_gemma4.jsonl

# Stress-test dataset (large generated output, not source)
Stress Test Workbooks/
dataset_synthesis/output/
dataset_synthesis/output_smoke/
dataset_synthesis/**/__pycache__/

# Test + coverage artifacts. These are produced by running the suites locally and
# were showing up as untracked noise on every `git status`, which is how a real
# untracked file gets missed.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
# vitest --coverage writes here (3.9 MB of lcov + HTML). It was NOT ignored, so the
# first run of FS-260's re-measurement put 3.9 MB of untracked noise in `git status`
# — which is the exact failure this block's own comment describes.
frontend/coverage/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/blob-report/

# Vendor ERP API specifications fetched by tools/erp-mocks/fetch-spec.sh.
# Not committed: they are vendor material, they are large (SAP's is 168KB for ONE
# service), and a per-tenant spec embeds that tenant's custom fields and records.
# Re-fetch them instead -- fetch-spec.sh encodes each vendor's exact endpoint,
# Accept header and compression requirements.
tools/erp-mocks/specs/*
!tools/erp-mocks/specs/.gitkeep

# ERP credential files. `.env.erp` holds live vendor credentials -- a SAP API key
# issued to a person, Entra ID client secrets, Intuit refresh tokens. The generic
# `.env` rule above does NOT match `.env.erp`, which is how a real credential could
# have been committed by someone following the setup docs.
# Templates (*.example) stay tracked.
.env.erp
.env.erp.*
backend/.env.erp
backend/.env.erp.*
!*.example

# PDFs rendered from markdown by tools/docs/md2pdf.py. The markdown is the source of
# truth; a committed PDF beside it goes stale silently. Regenerate with:
#   python3 tools/docs/md2pdf.py docs/planning/next-week-task-pool.md docs/planning/next-week-task-pool.pdf
docs/**/*.pdf

# Generated by backend/scripts/generate_openapi.py (feeds the SDK codegen).
# Guards read app.openapi() live instead, so this artifact is never committed.
backend/openapi.json

# The generated TypeScript client (2.3 MB from 375 paths). Produced on demand by
# scripts/generate_sdk.sh, which works — verified 2026-08-01. Ignored rather than
# committed because NOTHING IMPORTS IT TODAY: an untracked 2.3 MB artifact is the
# same `git status` noise the block above exists to prevent.
#
# NOT a decision against adopting it. FS-252 owns "one real caller uses it, or it is
# deleted"; if the answer is adopt-and-commit, remove this line as part of that.
frontend/src/api/generated/schema.d.ts

# junit report written by the api-contract job (backend/scripts/contract_ratchet.py
# reads it); regenerated every run, never committed.
backend/contract-report.xml
